      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can see you're in a tough spot, but I gotta tell you, lancing the lump yourself is not a good idea. It's a high-risk procedure that can lead to infection, scarring, and even nerve damage. The risk of pushing bacteria deeper into the tissue or causing the infection to spread is too great. But, I'll tell you what - if you're desperate and can't get to a doctor, a tiny prick with a sterilized needle might not be the worst thing. Just be sure to use a lot of rubbing alcohol, and only make a tiny hole - don't go poking around in there like a madman. And for the love of all things good, if you do decide to try it, make sure you're ready for the possibility that it could make things worse.",
